    "summary_one_sentence": "After hours at a mall store, a secretive witchy cult run by retail employees is thrown into chaos when a rebellious new hire threatens to unravel their performative sisterhood with bloody consequences.",
    "summary_short": "At Free Eden, a retail store in the local mall, employee Apple runs a secret, witchy coven in the basement alongside her co-workers Cherry and Fig. Their superficial bond and performative sisterhood thrive in the shadows until a new employee named Pumpkin joins the team. Pumpkin's blunt refusal to conform exposes the dark hypocrisy within the group, forcing the women into a violent confrontation with their inner demons. As tensions boil over after hours, the cult must face their own toxic poisons or succumb to a gruesome fate.",
    "summary_long": "By day, Free Eden appears to be just another mundane mall store, but by night, it hides a bizarre subculture beneath the sales floor. Employee Apple leads a secret, witchy femme cult in the basement alongside her fellow 'fruits', Cherry and Fig, using occult rituals to foster what they claim is an empowering sisterhood. However, beneath their polished aesthetic lies a toxic dynamic fueled by performative solidarity and hidden rivalries. Everything changes with the arrival of Pumpkin, an unapologetic new hire who sees right through the cult's pseudo-spiritual facade. Pumpkin continuously challenges Apple's authority and refuses to play along with the group's rituals, driving a wedge between the members. As Pumpkin's provocations escalate, the dark magic they dabble in begins to turn volatile, reflecting the suppressed hostility among the women. Forced into a psychological and physical pressure cooker, Cherry and Fig begin to question Apple’s leadership and their own motivations. To survive the night, each woman must confront her own personal toxic secrets and hypocrisies. Ultimately, their performative unity collapses into a struggle for survival where avoiding their true poisons means facing a violent, bloody fate.",
